<h2>Why the statutes diverge</h2>
<p>Maintenance law in India is a layered construction: a secular, summary remedy (Section 125 CrPC, now Section 144 BNSS) designed to prevent destitution; personal-law codes such as HAMA that distribute family obligations among Hindus; and a welfare statute for the elderly that deliberately widens every definition. Each was drafted with a paradigm family in mind, and the step-relationship tests the edges of all three. The result is that the same household can yield different answers depending on which door is knocked.</p>

<table class="law">
